# Design System + MUI

## Must use

- MUI + `sx` prop only — **no** `.css`, `.scss`, or CSS modules
- Theme from `src/design-system/theme` via `ThemeProvider`
- Tokens from `src/design-system/tokens` (colors, typography, spacing, layout)
- Shared primitives from `@/design-system` or `@/components/ui` before creating new ones
- Extract repeated styles to `ComponentName.styles.ts`

## Do not

- Override shared UI with inline styles or deep selectors
- Hardcode one-off colors/fonts when a token exists
- Import raw MUI for patterns already wrapped (`UiButton`, `UiContainer`, `UiSection`, `UiHeading`, `UiText`)
- Use Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system font stacks for brand UI

## Example

```tsx
// ✅
import { UiButton, UiHeading } from '@/design-system'
import { sectionStyles } from './Section.styles'

<UiHeading sx={sectionStyles.title}>Zimam</UiHeading>
<UiButton size="large">Explore</UiButton>

// ❌
import Button from '@mui/material/Button'
<button style={{ color: '#209E94' }}>Explore</button>
```

## Visual direction

Dark hero + light body joined by a soft lime glow (no hard section borders). Ink neutrals, lime accent (`#AFFC41`), Syne + DM Sans. Avoid purple themes and cream/terracotta looks.
